# Provenance of merge/mbxr_engine.v
#
# Copied from engine revision 2a and then edited to instantiate the two lanes.  The md5s
# below are of the SOURCE files at the time of the copy, so a later change to revision 2a
# is visible as a mismatch here and can be re-merged deliberately.  They are NOT the md5s
# of the files Vivado reads -- the build log prints those as ENGINE_RTL: lines.
#
# 2026-09-18: mbxr_tseq.v and mbxr_datapath.v re-recorded for the 6-bit weight unpacker
# (B80).  The PREVIOUS values -- the ones 0x5A5A002E md5 d6112edd was built from -- are
# 8596f212d1e9b05e6bad4d2ce8911929 (mbxr_tseq.v) and 6c6aa1b8375528fd20f0aa18dddc6e30
# (mbxr_datapath.v), with merge/mbxr_engine.v itself at cce8c84fde25710ad4bb860c6f1c83cf.
# A build log carrying the NEW md5s contains the unpacker; one carrying the old ones does not.
#
# NOT MINE AND LEFT ALONE: rtl_study/roccmoon/mbxr_engine.v's entry below was ALREADY moved
# before the unpacker landed (recorded 38adce9a, on disk fcde3f34 at 0x5A5A002E's build).  That
# is revision 2a's own engine, which the `lanes` variant does not read, and re-recording it
# here would bury a pre-existing drift inside an unrelated change.

